l find during the week but until the  officials are evaluated on these plays  that ok this is going to affect my  postseason if I don't call this I don't  think you're gonna see very many of  these they put the words in bracing for  contact for runners yeah and I think I  think that's kind of a dog whistle two  officials that  runner you can always bail out and not  make a call by saying I felt in  real-time  he was bracing for contact but clearly  not what happened on this point what are  we looking at the officials with these  roughing the passer calls it feels like  they've been told to call it enforce it  and you don't want to get downgraded so  it feels like the officials went above  and beyond the call of duty or am I  reading too much into it  no I think that was that was absolutely  true in the first three weeks if I'm not  mistaken there were only four in week  week four yeah and I think three of them  were in one game and only one of the  four I believe was body weight which was  a clear and obvious foul in the San  Francisco Chargers game so I you know  it's tough to say after one week whether  you know it's because players have  adjusted although I do think that is the  case I see a lot of adjustment on  defensive players as they hit the  quarterbacks now or or if the referees  have have indeed backed off somewhat and  and and have a little more discretion or  a combination thereof are you told you  know explicitly protect the quarterback  is that yeah there's no question that is  the referees number-one priority it has  it was in 1998 in 2001 when I became a  referee and it continues into this year  there's no question that's their number  one priority is this for ratings well I  I think it's for you know and the NFL is  an entertainment business and the game  is better with the starting quarterbacks  in you've got 32 quarterbacks that are  extremely important most of them are the  franchise player of the team and and  that's who they want to stay in th