ler might  have been in that in that in that mode  Phil Rivers might might might fall into  that category but really all of them all  of them do it I mean I and I say all of  them I I see let's put this way I've  seen everyone do it at least once  to be fair do refs want to do interviews  after the game no absolutely not  that is that is one of the worst ideas I  think I've ever heard in my life we want  you interviewed after the game would  make it would make for great  television no doubt you've been under  the microscope and have people talking  about you and complaining about you for  three hours and now we're gonna further  that by putting you under the spotlight  without having access to any video and  all you're going to do is is try to  justify defend what you've seen and what  you saw in real time and and you may or  may not be right so I don't think it  serves any purpose whatsoever from from  a being productive in explaining what's  what what's happening Terry you  mentioned the magic magic words it's  great for TV  we're in the entertainment business but  but the officials are not they're not  supposed to be the ones that that are  attacked and and that has to have to  make that make your story for you good  to visit with you safe travels to Dallas  and great to catch up with you again  Terry thank you for your time thanks for  having me Dan Terry McCauley NBC rules  analyst for more Dan Patrick show to the  audience Channel 239 on DirecTV or  download the Dan Patrick show app  [Music]

